Subject: [PATCH] libcalamaresui: retranslate QML view steps

QML view steps are loaded asynchronously during startup, before the user can
select a language on the welcome page. Their qsTr() bindings therefore keep
the live session's language unless the QQmlEngine is explicitly told to
retranslate them after Calamares installs a different translator.

Connect each QmlViewStep engine to Calamares' retranslation signal, matching
the existing behavior of the QML slideshow.

Fixes: https://github.com/Nobara-Project/rpm-sources/issues/577

diff --git a/src/libcalamaresui/viewpages/QmlViewStep.cpp b/src/libcalamaresui/viewpages/QmlViewStep.cpp
--- a/src/libcalamaresui/viewpages/QmlViewStep.cpp
+++ b/src/libcalamaresui/viewpages/QmlViewStep.cpp
@@ -17,6 +17,7 @@
 #include "utils/Logger.h"
 #include "utils/NamedEnum.h"
 #include "utils/Qml.h"
+#include "utils/Retranslator.h"
 #include "utils/Variant.h"
 #include "widgets/WaitingWidget.h"
 
@@ -88,6 +89,8 @@ QmlViewStep::QmlViewStep( QObject* parent )
 
     m_qmlEngine->addImportPath( Calamares::qmlModulesDir().absolutePath() );
 
+    CALAMARES_RETRANSLATE( if ( m_qmlEngine ) { m_qmlEngine->retranslate(); } );
+
     // QML Loading starts when the configuration for the module is set.
 }
 
